        "original_id": "17692fee-f133-5a00-841a-d9e45b5ba0f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke\n- Organizations: School of the Air, Royal Flying Doctor Service\n- Places: South Australia, Australia\n- Concepts: correspondence schooling, radio-based education, internet-based education\n\nFacts:\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was born on 8 June 1881 and died on 4 February 1962.\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was a South Australian educator and teacher.\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was pivotal in the formation of the School of the Air using the existing Royal Flying Doctor Service radio network.\n- School of the Air is a generic term for correspondence schools serving primary and early secondary children in remote and outback Australia.\n- School of the Air traditionally conducted some or all classes by radio.\n- School of the Air has been replacing radio-based classes with internet technology.",
